00:32.370 --> 00:35.370
So there are steps, a step-by-step set of instructions

00:35.370 --> 00:36.540
for what I'd like you to do

00:36.540 --> 00:39.360
starting with make a new folder called shopping,

00:39.360 --> 00:41.460
initialize a new git repo inside of it,

00:41.460 --> 00:43.860
make sure you're not already in a git repo,

00:43.860 --> 00:47.040
and then make a new file called yard.txt,

00:47.040 --> 00:49.830
then make a second file groceries.txt,

00:49.830 --> 00:53.220
make a commit that includes both empty files.

00:53.220 --> 00:55.110
So a commit with both of those files.

00:55.110 --> 00:57.870
And then I tell you the exact message you should use,

00:57.870 --> 00:59.970
and if you deviate from that, it's not a big deal.

00:59.970 --> 01:03.120
But anyway, I'm just putting it there

01:03.120 --> 01:04.500
if you wanna follow that.

01:04.500 --> 01:07.590
And then make some changes in the yard.txt file,

01:07.590 --> 01:09.060
we actually add some content

01:09.060 --> 01:11.010
and then we add some content to the groceries.

01:11.010 --> 01:13.110
And you can just copy and paste from here.

01:13.110 --> 01:15.030
And then make a second commit,

01:15.030 --> 01:18.750
including only the changes from the groceries file.

01:18.750 --> 01:20.767
And the message for the commit should say

01:20.767 --> 01:23.160
"Add ingredients for tomato soup."

01:23.160 --> 01:24.660
Then make a second commit

01:24.660 --> 01:28.230
including only the changes from the yard file.

01:28.230 --> 01:32.070
And that message should say add items needed for garden box.

01:32.070 --> 01:33.300
And then next up

01:33.300 --> 01:35.940
we're going to make some changes to both files.

01:35.940 --> 01:39.420
We're going to add this line to the end of the yard file.

01:39.420 --> 01:41.430
